.\" readlink.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX readlink(1) utility,
.\" which this tree does not provide. An original page (this
.\" project's own text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT
.\" like the code, same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in
.\" docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the
.\" omission is not re-litigated. Rendered at build time to
.\" build/man/READLINK.TXT and staged on the play image as
.\" /usr/man/READLINK.
.TH READLINK 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
readlink \- print the resolved value of a symbolic link
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Readlink
is not provided on maux.
ProDOS has no hard links, no symbolic links, and no named pipes
(docs/ANACHRONISMS.md sec W2).
